    structure: "Two or more emergency identities exist outside the normal directory synchronisation and outside conditional access policy, so a policy mistake or an identity provider outage cannot lock them. Their credentials are strong (hardware keys or long random secrets) and stored sealed, split between two custodians or in a physical safe with a tamper evident envelope. Any sign in or use of these identities triggers an alert to several administrators who did not perform the action. The person using the account records a justification before or immediately after. After use, credentials are rotated, the envelope is replaced, and a review within days confirms the use was warranted and records what was done. The accounts are tested on a schedule to prove they still work and are still excluded from policies that have changed since.",
