    underStress: "It is designed for stress and gets more valuable as everything else fails, provided it was tested when things were calm. It fails under stress when the sealed credential is stale, when the alert channel depends on the system that is down, or when the only custodian is unreachable. Strength depends on redundancy of accounts, custodians and alert channels.",
    adoption: "Create two emergency identities today and exclude them from every conditional policy by explicit rule. Store credentials in a physical safe or split between two custodians, not in the same tooling the accounts are meant to rescue. Wire sign in alerts to a channel that several administrators watch and that does not depend on the identity provider. Write the justification and review procedure in one page. Test quarterly and after every policy change, then use the confidence to shorten normal access durations.",
